### Keep in English (do not translate)
- TechCorp Inc.
- Blue Aurum Financial
- ABC Robots
- FreshLane Markets
- XYZ Retail Store
- GFM Bank
- ABC Corp

### Reason
Maintain consistency with original materials and facilitate cross-reference

---

## 9. SPECIFIC TRANSLATION PATTERNS

### Common Phrases
- "In this lab" → "Neste laboratório"
- "Step-by-step instructions" → "Instruções passo a passo"
- "Click here" → "Clique aqui"
- "Please find" → "Você encontrará" or "Acesse"
- "The following" → "O seguinte" or "A seguir"
- "As shown below" → "Como mostrado abaixo"
- "For example" → "Por exemplo"
- "Note that" → "Note que" or "Observe que"

### Tone and Voice
- Use professional but accessible tone
- Prefer active voice
- Avoid unnecessary jargon
- Maintain clarity and objectivity

### Numbers and Metrics
- Keep original format (e.g., 30%, $1M, 100k)
- Use period for thousands in Portuguese when appropriate
- Keep units in English when international standard (GB, MB, etc.)

---

## 10. FILE STRUCTURE

### Folder Organization
```
usecases/
├── case-name/
│   ├── README.md (main, in Portuguese)
│   ├── assets/ (images, diagrams)
│   │   ├── screenshots/
│   │   └── diagrams/
│   ├── labs/ or practitioner_docs/
│   │   └── hands-on-lab.md (detailed instructions)
│   └── src/ (code, if applicable)
```

### File Naming
- Use kebab-case: `file-name.md`
- Avoid spaces and special characters
- Prefer descriptive names in English for technical files
- READMEs always in Portuguese

---

## 11. LINKS AND REFERENCES

### Internal Links
- Always use relative paths
- Format: `[Text](./relative/path.md)`
- Verify links work after translation

### External Links
- Keep original URLs
- Add Portuguese context when necessary
- Example: `[Official documentation](https://url) (in English)`

### Video References
- Keep original video URLs
- Add Portuguese description
- Preferred format:
```markdown
## 🎥 Demonstração

[▶️ Assistir à demonstração](VIDEO_URL)
```

---

## 12. CODE AND EXAMPLES HANDLING

### Code Blocks
- Keep code in English (variables, functions, technical comments)
- Translate only explanatory comments when appropriate
- Maintain original formatting and indentation

### CLI Commands
- Keep commands exactly as in original
- Add Portuguese explanations before or after
- Example:
```markdown
Execute o seguinte comando:
```bash
npm install
```
```

### Data Examples
- Keep original JSON/YAML structure
- Translate only example values when it makes sense
- Keep keys in English

---

## 13. QUALITY AND REVIEW

### Quality Checklist
- [ ] All technical terms follow translation rules
- [ ] README structure follows defined pattern
- [ ] Internal links work correctly
- [ ] Images have alt text
- [ ] Appropriate emojis in titles
- [ ] Professional and consistent tone
- [ ] No Portuguese errors
- [ ] Correct markdown formatting
- [ ] Code and commands kept in English
- [ ] Fictional company names not translated
- [ ] Agent names without special characters

### Final Review
Before considering complete:
1. Read complete document
2. Verify all links
3. Test commands (if applicable)
4. Validate images load
5. Confirm structure consistent with other use cases

---

## 14. SPECIAL CASES

### Acronyms
- First mention: translation + English acronym
  - Example: "Geração Aumentada por Recuperação (RAG)"
- Subsequent mentions: acronym only
  - Example: "O sistema RAG permite..."

### Direct Quotes
- Keep in English with Portuguese translation in parentheses if needed
- Use quotes or quote block

### Tables
- Translate headers
- Keep technical content in English when appropriate
- Example:
```markdown
| Caso de Uso | Features |
|-------------|----------|
| Ask HR | `RAG` `Multi-agent` |
```

---

## 15. VERSIONING AND MAINTENANCE

### Update Comments
Add at top of updated files:
```markdown
<!-- Last update: YYYY-MM-DD -->
<!-- Based on: agentic-ai-client-bootcamp version X.X -->
```

### Change Tracking
- Document significant changes
- Maintain update history when relevant
- Reference source version when applicable

### Reviewing Existing Use Cases
When updating the bootcamp repository with new content from source:
1. **Compare versions**: Check source repository for updates to existing use cases
2. **Identify changes**: Look for new features, updated screenshots, improved explanations
3. **Prioritize updates**: Focus on content changes over minor formatting
4. **Maintain consistency**: Apply .bobrules to updated content
5. **Test links**: Verify all internal and external links still work
6. **Update features tags**: Add new feature tags if capabilities were added
7. **Check images**: Ensure screenshots reflect current UI state
8. **Validate translations**: Confirm technical terms follow terminology rules

**Review Checklist for Existing Use Cases:**
- [ ] Content matches latest source version
- [ ] All .bobrules applied (structure, emojis, formatting)
- [ ] Images optimized and loading correctly
- [ ] Links functional (internal and external)
- [ ] Feature tags updated and accurate
- [ ] Technical terminology consistent
- [ ] No translation errors or inconsistencies
- [ ] Hands-on labs tested and working

---

**These rules must be followed consistently across all bootcamp documents.**
**When in doubt, consult existing examples or this document.**